WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Welcome to Cedar Crossing, our fictional practice library.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.675
Avery has just been promoted to service coordinator.

3
00:00:06.816 --> 00:00:12.298
Yesterday, Avery was the person who could untangle almost any meeting-room reservation.

4
00:00:12.438 --> 00:00:17.594
Today, Avery is responsible for helping a whole team provide that service reliably.

5
00:00:17.735 --> 00:00:21.225
The opening scene shows Avery listening around a worktable.

6
00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:27.356
A room-booking update is coming, staff need training, and families still need help reserving spaces.

7
00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:34.366
Avery's first instinct is to redesign the instructions, answer every question, and fix every mistake personally.

8
00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:39.589
But if every problem waits for Avery, the team becomes dependent on one busy person.

9
00:00:39.729 --> 00:00:45.492
Our question is: how do you move from being good at your own job to helping an entire team succeed?

10
00:00:45.632 --> 00:00:48.335
Chapter twenty-one explores this transition.

11
00:00:48.475 --> 00:00:53.260
We will follow Avery through choices about trust, shared work, and professional growth.

12
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.002
Cedar Crossing is invented for practice.

13
00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:58.575
The Westfield case is your separate reading.

14
00:00:58.715 --> 00:01:02.645
You can listen, read, revisit any segment, or skip an activity.
